#
# Build the indices (version 2)
#
# This version seeks to unify the handling of index items among many lists,
# including handling extracting MPI names into separate lists that can be
# compared with (and perhaps eventually used as) lists in the text.
#
# Structure of input:
#   \indexentry{[NAME[=VAL]:]entry[@formated name][!entry[@formated name]]|type-of-link}{page-number}
#   \indexentry{NEWEXAMPLES:number::languages::desc::handlelist|type-of-link}{page-number}
#
# Things that need to be fixed in the input:
#   Functions with arguments in the entry, e.g., MPI\_Send(....)
#   Remove non-main entry when there is a primary entry on the same page
# Things that need to be checked
#   Detect invalid characters in input
#   Too many sub entries (only three levels, i.e., two "!" in list
#   Unknown link type (only hyperpage or hyperindexformat{...})
#
#
#
# Outline of implementation
# Set defaults, collect commandline args
# Read index file (from LaTeX)
#    Parse each entry to:
#        Extract type-of-list, prefix, entry text
#        Parse type-of-list
#        1. Simple items, append to list
#        2. Special cases, process (NEWEXAMPLES requires special routine,
#           other const/handle types just go to const
#        3. If requested, create lists of symbols
#        4. If entry is primary, add the page number to a dict of primaries
#           for each of the 5 indicies. Add both the full entry (e.g., with
#           all subentries) and the top level name.
#
# Check for primary definition and remove non-primary ref on same page as
# primary ref
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Output idx files and constlist files
#
# -
